    "created_at": "2024-07-07T13:02:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-07T13:02:46Z",
    "body": "Ah okay, that's good info. That's also pretty much how [Firefox does it](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/base/TimeoutManager.cpp#455). \r\n\r\nBy the way, I spotted some Undefined Behaviour in that Chromium code (signed int overflow), which [I've sent in a patch for](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/5681342).\r\n\r\nThe Firefox code is also technically broken, because the value can overflow and use the ID 0, or reuse ID's. (The [webIDL types](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/webidl/WindowOrWorkerGlobalScope.webidl) should probably also be changed to unsigned long).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
